2026-07-23 20:08:53,675 - src.research_handler - INFO - Query: Act as an experienced political researcher, investigative journalist, policy analyst, and legal expert. Prepare a comprehensive and unbiased report on CJP in India. First identify which CJP is being referred to: 1. Citizens for Justice and Peace (Human Rights Organization) OR 2. Cockroach Janta Party (Youth Movement / Political Protest) If both exist, explain both separately. Generate a detailed report with the following sections. SECTION 1 Executive Summary - What is CJP? - Why was it created? - Why is it currently important? SECTION 2 History - Founding year - Founders - Timeline - Major milestones SECTION 3 Objectives - Mission - Vision - Core values - Main demands SECTION 4 Leadership - Key leaders - Organizational structure - Decision-making process SECTION 5 Activities - Major campaigns - Public movements - Legal actions - Awareness programs - Community work SECTION 6 Political Position - Is it a political party? - Is it an NGO? - Is it a social movement? - Does it contest elections? - Which ideologies influence it? SECTION 7 Public Support - Youth support - Student support - Academic support - Civil society support - Criticism SECTION 8 Government Response - Statements - Court cases - Police actions - Government negotiations - Policy responses SECTION 9 Media Coverage - National media - International media - Social media trends - Viral campaigns SECTION 10 Controversies - Major allegations - Public criticism - Responses from the organization - Fact-checks SECTION 11 Legal Status - Registration details - Applicable laws - Court proceedings - Constitutional issues SECTION 12 Funding - Sources of funding - Donations - Transparency - Financial disclosures (if available) SECTION 13 Impact - Successes - Failures - Public opinion - Influence on Indian society - Influence on policy SECTION 14 Comparison Compare CJP with: - Aam Aadmi Party - BJP - INC - NSUI - ABVP - Other student or civil society organizations SECTION 15 Future Outlook - Possible future scenarios - Challenges - Opportunities - Expected impact over the next five years SECTION 16 Timeline Create a chronological timeline of important events. SECTION 17 Frequently Asked Questions Answer at least 20 FAQs. SECTION 18 Key Statistics Include available statistics on: - Membership - Protests - Public participation - Donations - Social media reach SECTION 19 Fact Check Separate: - Verified facts - Claims - Allegations - Rumors - Unknown or disputed information SECTION 20 References List official websites, government documents, court judgments, credible news reports, and academic sources used. Requirements: - Maintain complete neutrality. - Clearly distinguish facts from opinions. - Cite sources for every major claim. - Present information in professional report format using tables where useful. - Mention whenever evidence is unavailable or disputed.
